    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 79c7c909a9c134939fe845de730f5dab8c581f08 -->\n**Review of head `79c7c909a`: clean.** A gate-runner that wrote neither commit checked the delta as text and ran the head on a merge with main `4dba7019d` (merge `5086c0f31`, not pushed).\n\n- **The delta `418e88034..79c7c909a`** moves the eight arguments of `tilted_wall` into the struct `TiltedWall` (same order, same values in each call). No assert, no number and no test name changes value. The other edits are format and comments. The diff has the same size with and without `-w`: no change of line ends.\n- **Tests:** `tests_tilted` 3 passed (`tilted_wall_builder_at_zero_tilt_is_a_z_hole`, `tilted_holes_in_a_plate_are_not_drilled_along_z`, `a_tilt_the_fit_accepts_moves_no_wall_past_fit_tol`); the `drilling` module 61 passed; the motion lib 570 passed.\n- **clippy** `-p camcraft-motion --all-targets -D warnings`: clean. (PR #3651, the same pin with no fix, was red on this step.)\n- **Mutation:** with `FIT_TOL` set to 0.5 the test `tilted_holes_in_a_plate_are_not_drilled_along_z` fails (\"a tilted hole must not pass as a Z hole\"). With 0.02 it passes. The pin guards the fit.\n\nNo product code changes. The merge waits for the post-merge run of `main` at `4dba7019d` (a batch of four merges); it closes #3554.\n",
